---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import {
  AgentFanoutMany,
  AgentFanoutPlayground,
  AgentFanoutStates,
  AgentFanoutTree,
} from "../../components/AgentFanoutDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Agent Fanout"
  description="A parent agent handing one task to subagents, live."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Agent Fanout</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A parent agent splits one task across subagents and merges what they find. A
    pulse runs down each line when a subagent starts and back up when it
    finishes.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><AgentFanoutPlayground client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Agent Fanout usage"
      code={`import { AgentFanout } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/agent-fanout";
import { Globe } from "reicon-react/icons/Globe";
import { ChartLine } from "reicon-react/icons/ChartLine";

<AgentFanout
  task="Choose a vector store for the retrieval stack"
  agents={[
    {
      id: "researcher",
      name: "Researcher",
      icon: <Globe size={16} />,
      task: "Web search",
      result: "Found 18 sources",
      status: "done",
      duration: 3000,
    },
    {
      id: "analyst",
      name: "Analyst",
      icon: <ChartLine size={16} />,
      task: "Benchmarks",
      status: "working",
    },
  ]}
  elapsed={elapsed}
  onStop={stop}
  onRestart={runAgain}
/>`}
    />
    <p>
      Your app owns the clock. Move each agent's <code>status</code> from <code
        >queued</code
      > to <code>working</code>, then to <code>done</code> or <code>failed</code
      >. Each change sends a pulse in the agent's color: down on <code
        >working</code
      >, up on <code>done</code>. The node lights up when the pulse lands.
    </p>
    <p>
      Set <code>state="done"</code> once the parent has merged the results. The center
      node turns into a check. After Stop, set <code>state="stopped"</code> and mark
      the agents that did not finish as <code>stopped</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The footer names the phase from the statuses: Delegating work, Specialists
      working, Merging results, Composing answer. Pass <code>label</code> to replace
      it. <code>elapsed</code> is in ms. <code>duration</code> shows on a row once
      the agent is done, and <code>result</code> replaces its task text.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Failed and stopped</h2>
    <p>
      A failed agent shows a red warning node and its <code>result</code> as the reason.
      Stopped agents fade.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4"><AgentFanoutStates client:visible /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">More agents</h2>
    <p>
      The graph is drawn with React Flow at a fixed zoom, so text stays full
      size. Columns share the width. Nodes shrink to fit, and names cut off with
      an ellipsis. Six agents still fit on a phone.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4"><AgentFanoutMany client:visible /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Nested subagents</h2>
    <p>
      Give an agent its own <code>agents</code> and it fans out again, one row per
      level. Helpers take their parent's color. Leaves share the width, and each parent
      sits over the middle of its helpers. The details list indents helpers under
      their parent. Pass <code>defaultOpen</code> to show the list at first.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4"><AgentFanoutTree client:visible /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The graph is decoration and is hidden from screen readers. The Details
      button says how many agents finished. It opens a list with each agent's
      name, task, and status. The footer phase is a live status, so changes are
      read out. The timer is not, so it does not interrupt. With reduced motion,
      pulses do not run and states change at once. In forced colors mode the
      lines and nodes use the system text color.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Agent colors cycle through <code>--sprout-chart-1</code> to <code
        >--sprout-chart-10</code
      >, or come from an agent's <code>color</code>. A finished node draws its
      check in <code>--sprout-surface</code> on the color. The card uses <code
        >--sprout-line</code
      > and <code>--sprout-surface</code>, like Card. The center node uses <code
        >--sprout-primary</code
      >. Set <code>--sprout-agent-fanout-trip</code> on the component to change how
      long a pulse takes (720ms).
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
